The Concise Data Lifecycle

    API Endpoint Gate

        The client hits /restaurants/chat with a RequirementHybridSearchRequest carrying the text query + a list of restaurant_ids.

        The controller performs Pydantic validation and passes the payload directly to the RestaurantService.

    The Orchestration Trigger

        RestaurantService receives the request and immediately invokes your dedicated RestaurantAgentOrchestrator service class, passing the raw string variables.

        answer = await agent_orchestrator.run_pipeline(query, restaurant_ids)

    CrewAI Routing (The Intent Gate)

        The orchestrator boots up the Multi-Agent Crew using a strict sequential workflow.

        Agent 1 (Intent Classifier): Analyzes the raw text to verify the request is an experiential search, then routes the context forward to the next task.

    The Tool Execution Bubble (Micro-Service Layer)

        Agent 2 (Requirements Agent): Detects qualitative vibes in the text and triggers the ID-Bounded Search Tool, passing it the query text and the restaurant_ids array.

        Inside the Tool (Sequential Business Logic):

            A. Embedding Adapter: Converts the text string into a mathematical coordinate array vector.

            B. Mongo Repository: Executes .vector_search_within_ids(), running an Atlas $vectorSearch query restricted strictly to the passed restaurant_ids.

            C. Re-ranker Adapter: Intercepts the top 20 raw results from MongoDB and runs cross-encoder sorting, slicing it down to the absolute best 5 precision matches.

            D. Serialization: Converts those 5 clean entities into plain text prose and hands them back to the crew.

    Synthesis & Response Packaging

        Agent 3 (Answer Generator): Receives the hyper-focused, pre-sorted 5 restaurant data points. It writes the personalized markdown explanation (AI Rationale) detailing exactly why these spots fit the user's needs.

        The orchestrator catches this final text, bundles it alongside the structured data models, and returns a unified HybridSearchResponse back to the UI.

